---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About - Harshana Moorthy">
  <section class="py-20">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-8">About Me</h1>
      
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-8">
          VP of Solution Engineering at AppViewX, leading a global team of solution engineers 
          across North America, EMEA, and APAC in the machine identity and PKI space.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-[#EFE9E1] p-8 rounded-lg mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Current Focus</h2>
          <ul class="space-y-3">
            <li className="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span className="text-[#4B00FF] text-xl">→</span>
              <span>Leading enterprise PKI/CLM transformation initiatives at Fortune 500 companies</span>
            </li>
            <li className="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span className="text-[#4B00FF] text-xl">→</span>
              <span>Post-quantum cryptography readiness and hybrid certificate strategies</span>
            </li>
            <li className="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span className="text-[#4B00FF] text-xl">→</span>
              <span>Building and scaling global SE teams across multiple geographies</span>
            </li>
            <li className="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span className="text-[#4B00FF] text-xl">→</span>
              <span>HSM-as-a-Service and cloud-native certificate management architectures</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Journey</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          I've spent my entire 10+ year career at AppViewX, progressing from SE intern through various 
          technical roles to my current position as VP of Solution Engineering. This journey has given me 
          a unique perspective on both the technical depth and the go-to-market motion required to succeed 
          in enterprise security software.
        </p>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          My path included roles as Customer Success Engineer, Senior SE, Enterprise Solutions Architect, 
          and Lead Principal Solutions Architect before stepping into leadership. This hands-on foundation 
          means I still write code, design architectures, and run POCs alongside my team.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 mt-8">Expertise Areas</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-8">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-2 text-[#4B00FF]">Technical</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-700">
              <li>• PKI architecture and certificate lifecycle management</li>
              <li>• ACME, EST, SCEP, CMP protocols</li>
              <li>• Post-quantum cryptography (ML-KEM, ML-DSA)</li>
              <li>• Kubernetes and cloud-native security</li>
              <li>• HSM integration and code signing</li>
              <li>• IoT certificate management at scale</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-2 text-[#4B00FF]">Leadership & GTM</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-700">
              <li>• SE team building and scaling (6→14 members)</li>
              <li>• POC/POV design and delivery</li>
              <li>• Partner enablement programs</li>
              <li>• RFP strategy and competitive positioning</li>
              <li>• Technical sales methodology</li>
              <li>• Cross-functional collaboration (Product, CS, AE)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 mt-8">Beyond Work</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          Based in Austin, Texas. Expecting our first child in August 2026. When I'm not working on 
          certificate management problems, I'm exploring AI applications for sales engineering productivity, 
          building tools to make complex security concepts more accessible, and staying current on the 
          latest developments in cryptography and identity management.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-white border-2 border-[#4B00FF] p-8 rounded-lg mt-8">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">Let's Connect</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Interested in discussing PKI, post-quantum cryptography, SE team building, or potential 
            collaboration opportunities? I'm always happy to connect with others in the space.
          </p>
          <div class="flex gap-4">
            <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/harshana-moorthy-savvy101/" 
               target="_blank" 
               rel="noopener noreferrer"
               class="bg-[#4B00FF] text-white px-6 py-2 rounded-lg hover:bg-[#3a00cc] transition-colors">
              LinkedIn
            </a>
            <a href="mailto:harshana.stude@gmail.com" 
               class="border-2 border-[#4B00FF] text-[#4B00FF] px-6 py-2 rounded-lg hover:bg-[#4B00FF] hover:text-white transition-colors">
              Email
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
